---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { repository, url } from '../lib/site';
import courtyard from '../assets/living-guide.png';
import cluster from '../assets/living-collaborate.png';
import canopy from '../assets/living-grow.png';
const places = [
  { image: courtyard, number: '01', title: 'Guide every change.', text: 'Neighbours notice problems and suggest ideas. You decide which projects to approve.' },
  { image: cluster, number: '02', title: 'Build together.', text: 'Give neighbours a small project budget. The co-op can improve services while you shape the homes.' },
  { image: canopy, number: '03', title: 'Let it grow.', text: 'Delegate more freedom. Watch residents add rooms and improve their surroundings, then inspect the tradeoffs.' },
];
---
<Base>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="wrap relative grid items-center gap-4 overflow-hidden pb-12 pt-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:pb-20 lg:pt-18">
      <div class="relative z-10 pb-4 lg:pb-10">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-7 flex items-center gap-2.5"><span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-forest"></span> A community simulation, open to everyone</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(3.5rem,6.4vw,6.3rem)] leading-[1.04] font-medium tracking-[-0.055em]">Small places.<br /><span class="text-forest">Big possibilities.</span></h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">What happens when a world has ideas of its own? Generate a community, build alongside its residents, and explore three possible futures.</p>
        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="button button-primary" href={url('play/')}>Play in your browser <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={url('docs/getting-started/')}>Start exploring <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
        <p class="mt-5 text-xs text-muted">Free to play. Open source. Yours to experiment with.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="relative -mx-6 sm:-mx-10 lg:-mr-24 lg:-ml-10">
        <div class="absolute top-[15%] left-[13%] h-[70%] w-[73%] rounded-full bg-leaf/55 blur-3xl"></div>
        <Image src={courtyard} alt="A generated in-game community with editable room interiors and shared utilities, shown after one simulated month." width={1120} height={840} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" class="relative w-full mix-blend-multiply" />
        <figcaption class="absolute right-[12%] bottom-[10%] flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-line bg-paper/95 px-4 py-3 shadow-sm"><span class="grid size-8 place-items-center rounded-full bg-leaf text-forest" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><div><span class="block text-xs font-semibold">One place. Many possible futures.</span><span class="text-[11px] text-muted">Living worlds · playable prototype</span></div></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <div class="border-y border-line bg-white/35"><div class="wrap flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-3 py-5 text-xs text-muted"><span>BUILT FOR CURIOSITY</span><span>18–24 neighbours</span><span>One year of possibilities</span><span>Rules you can remix</span><span class="font-semibold text-forest">MIT licensed ↗</span></div></div>
    <section class="wrap py-20 lg:py-28">
      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-end"><div><p class="eyebrow mb-4">A small world with real tradeoffs</p><h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">One beginning.<br />Three possible futures.</h2></div><p class="max-w-lg text-base leading-relaxed text-muted md:justify-self-end">These scenes began with the same homes, people and weather. After one simulated month, different freedoms leave different marks. Switch between futures to find out who benefits and what it costs.</p></div>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {places.map((place) => <article><div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line bg-[#eeeedf]"><span class="absolute top-4 left-4 z-10 font-mono text-xs text-muted">{place.number} / ONE MONTH LATER</span><Image src={place.image} alt={`${place.title} A scene rendered by the Courtyard Block game.`} width={560} height={420} loading="lazy" class="w-full mix-blend-multiply transition-transform duration-500 hover:scale-[1.035]" /></div><h3 class="mt-6 font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight">{place.title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{place.text}</p></article>)}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="bg-ink py-20 text-paper"><div class="wrap grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr] lg:gap-24"><div><p class="eyebrow mb-5 text-leaf/70!">A loop for curious minds</p><h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Try something.<br />Learn something.<br /><span class="text-[#b7d69c]">Try something else.</span></h2><p class="mt-6 max-w-sm text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/65">No perfect score to chase. Notice a problem, make a change, and discover the next question.</p></div><div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">{[
        ['01', 'Make a change', 'Find a seed you like. Snap on a room, move a home, or improve a shared service.'],
        ['02', 'Meet the unexpected', 'Advance a week. Read neighbours’ proposals and watch their permitted projects take shape.'],
        ['03', 'Follow the people', 'Look beyond averages. Find out who is cold, who can pay their bills, and where services struggle.'],
        ['04', 'Share a possibility', 'Keep your inputs and assumptions together. Send a complete experiment to a friend to remix.'],
      ].map(([number, title, text]) => <article><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[#b7d69c]">{number}</span><h3 class="mt-4 text-lg font-semibold">{title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/65">{text}</p></article>)}</div></div></section>
    <section class="wrap grid gap-12 py-20 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center lg:gap-24 lg:py-28">
      <div><p class="eyebrow mb-5">The best idea might be yours</p><h2 class="font-display text-4xl leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Make a world<br />worth sharing.</h2><p class="mt-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">Remix construction costs, resident priorities and project budgets in the living-world workshop. Import new wall materials, share your seed and decisions, or draft a kit with your favourite AI assistant.</p><div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="button button-primary" href={url('docs/living-worlds/')}>Remix a living world <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={repository}>Explore the source ↗</a></div></div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white/70 p-7 sm:p-10"><div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-line pb-5"><span class="eyebrow">A material is a starting point</span><span class="pill bg-leaf/50">Editable</span></div><div class="py-6"><span class="text-xs text-muted">YOUR NEXT EXPERIMENT</span><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl">A warmer kind of wall.</h3></div><dl class="space-y-0 text-sm">{[['Material layers', 'Timber + insulation'], ['Thermal properties', 'Defined by your data'], ['Costs & assumptions', 'Visible and inspectable'], ['Your evidence', 'Sources travel with the mod']].map(([label, value]) => <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-2 border-t border-line py-4"><dt class="text-muted">{label}</dt><dd class="font-medium">{value}</dd></div>)}</dl><p class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-paper p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">The same model runs every supported assembly. AI can help draft a pack; you decide which assumptions to test.</p></div>
    </section>
    <section class="wrap"><div class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-leaf/30 p-8 md:flex-row md:items-center md:p-12"><div><p class="eyebrow mb-3">A foundation we can build on</p><h2 class="font-display text-3xl tracking-tight">Open code. Open questions.</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">This is an early, bounded simulation. Today: generated communities, resident construction, heat, utilities, costs and one year of fixed households. The inputs are illustrative. More construction methods, richer community life and longer horizons are questions for the road ahead.</p></div><a class="button button-secondary shrink-0 bg-paper" href={url('docs/moddability/')}>Read the direction →</a></div></section>
  </main>
</Base>
